      "id": "how-ultrastable-two-loops",
      "surface": "site/worker.js",
      "text": "A system is ultrastable, in W. Ross Ashby's sense, when two loops keep its essential variables inside bounds: a fast loop that corrects disturbance, and a slow loop that changes the system itself when the fast loop cannot.",
